## A mirror sphere reflecting a matte sphere placed behind the camera, lit
## by one ambientlight, no Option naming an indirect-light pass: the
## baseline indirectseam_mirror_constant.rib compares against. The far
## sphere's placement, and Identity resetting the CTM before it, follow the
## same convention tests/rib/r8_mirror.rib uses for its wall. Its radius is
## large enough that the mirror's reflection fully covers several interior
## pixels, not only its rim. Not third-party.
Display "indirectseam_mirror_none.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 48 48 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.3931372549019608]

AttributeBegin
Identity
Translate 0 0 -10
Surface "matte" "Ka" [1] "Kd" [1]
Color [1 1 1]
Opacity [1 1 1]
Sides 2
Sphere 5 -5 5 360
AttributeEnd

AttributeBegin
Surface "mirror" "Kr" [1]
Color [1 1 1]
Opacity [1 1 1]
Sphere 1.2 -1.2 1.2 360
AttributeEnd

WorldEnd
